From 084f4b618b51cc5be84e969bbef8a305e268d337 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:02:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm: mediatek: Add MT6789 (Helio G99) SoC support

Add core SoC initialization, TrustZone/EMI-MPU-safe ARMv8 memory map,
and low-level boot framebuffer address capture for MediaTek MT6789
(Helio G99 / MT8781).

Secure EL3 (BL31), TrustZone TEE, SSPM, SCP/SPM/MCUPM, and RKP windows
are left unmapped in mt6789_mem_map[] to prevent Cortex-A76 speculative
prefetch bus firewall faults, and get_page_table_size() reserves 256 KiB
so runtime 4 KiB-aligned simple-framebuffer remapping can split 2 MiB
block descriptors cleanly.

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
---
